{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "41d5f312",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "title: \"SAR processing with openEO\"\n",
    "resources:\n",
    "  - sar_processing_viewer.js\n",
    "  - sar_processing_viewer.webp\n",
    "jupyter: python3\n",
    "format:\n",
    "  html:\n",
    "    toc: true\n",
    "    page-layout: full\n",
    "execute:\n",
    "  cache: true\n",
    "  freeze: auto\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "Sentinel-1 radar backscatter can be processed \n",
    "in the cloud with openEO on the Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem.\n",
    "This guide calibrates the same Sentinel-1 data in two ways, \n",
    "**γ⁰ (gamma0, terrain-flattened)** and **σ⁰ (sigma0, ellipsoid)**, \n",
    "compares what each costs, and then compares the results on a map.\n",
    "\n",
    "For beginners in openEO and SAR processing, we recommend carefully reading\n",
    "through the first sections and trying to understand the difference in output.\n",
    "For advanced users, the last two sections contain background and details on \n",
    "used methods and options to finetune the output.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Two ways to calibrate backscatter\n",
    "\n",
    "Sentinel-1 GRD data is calibrated to backscatter in the `sar_backscatter` process. The `coefficient` argument decides how the signal is normalised:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `sigma0-ellipsoid` (σ⁰) normalises by the area on the ellipsoid. It needs no terrain flattening, so less processing is expected, but slopes facing the sensor look much brighter than slopes facing away from it.\n",
    "- `gamma0-terrain` (γ⁰) is radiometrically terrain-flattened. It needs an extra processing step, so more processing is expected, and it removes most of the slope-induced brightness differences.\n",
    "\n",
    "We run both for exactly the same area and period, first compare their cost in terms of credits and resources, and then look at how the output differs.\n",
    "The example is in a mountain area, which results in highest processing cost and output\n",
    "difference. Expect smaller differences in more flat areas.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Monthly composites over six months\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of a single composite, we take six months of data (May to October 2026)\n",
    "and compute one median composite **per month**. \n",
    "The result has six dates per pixel, which allows us to look \n",
    "at pixel time series later on. Each composite is \n",
    "in decibel (`10·log10`) and resampled to Web Mercator (EPSG:3857) for visualization purposes.\n",
    "\n",
    "The function below builds the monthly composite for a given backscatter coefficient, and exports the result to a workspace as a GeoTIFF per month and band, together with a STAC collection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "6cedbd2a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Authenticated using refresh token.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import openeo\n",
    "from openeo import collection_property\n",
    "\n",
    "connection = openeo.connect(\"openeo-staging.dataspace.copernicus.eu\").authenticate_oidc()\n",
    "\n",
    "bbox = [1397574.0, 5935182.0, 1455819.0, 5999236.0]\n",
    "# Test area: 1/10 of each side, around the centre\n",
    "# bbox = [1423784.25, 5964006.3, 1429608.75, 5970412.7]\n",
    "extent = dict(zip([\"west\", \"south\", \"east\", \"north\"], bbox), crs=\"EPSG:3857\")\n",
    "temporal_extent = [\"2026-05-01\", \"2026-11-01\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def monthly_composite(coefficient: str, **backscatter_args):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Monthly median backscatter composite in dB, in EPSG:3857 at 10 m.\n",
    "    Extra arguments are passed on to `sar_backscatter`, see the advanced parameters below.\"\"\"\n",
    "    cube = connection.load_collection(\n",
    "        \"SENTINEL1_GRD\",\n",
    "        spatial_extent=extent,\n",
    "        temporal_extent=temporal_extent,\n",
    "        bands=[\"VV\", \"VH\"],\n",
    "        properties=[\n",
    "            collection_property(\"sat:orbit_state\") == \"ascending\",\n",
    "            collection_property(\"sar:instrument_mode\") == \"IW\",\n",
    "        ],\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    cube = cube.sar_backscatter(coefficient=coefficient, **backscatter_args)\n",
    "    cube = cube.aggregate_temporal_period(\"month\", reducer=\"median\")\n",
    "    cube = cube.apply(lambda x: 10 * x.log(base=10))\n",
    "    return cube.resample_spatial(projection=3857, resolution=10)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "0af34f27",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: false\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "from IPython.display import HTML, Markdown\n",
    "from openeo.internal.jupyter import render_component\n",
    "\n",
    "def export_to_workspace(cube, collection: str):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Writes one COG per month and band, and merges their STAC items into the given collection.\"\"\"\n",
    "    result = cube.save_result(\n",
    "        format=\"GTiff\",\n",
    "        options=dict(filename_prefix=\"median_composite\", separate_asset_per_band=True),\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return result.process(\n",
    "        \"export_workspace\",\n",
    "        arguments={\"data\": result, \"workspace\": \"openeo-examples-workspace\", \"merge\": collection},\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_job(name: str, cube, collection: str) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Runs the export as a batch job once. The job id and metadata are cached in sar_processing_job_<name>.json,\n",
    "    so later renders can show the job without re-running or re-fetching it.\"\"\"\n",
    "    job_file = Path(f\"sar_processing_job_{name}.json\")\n",
    "    cache = json.loads(job_file.read_text()) if job_file.exists() else {}\n",
    "\n",
    "    if \"id\" not in cache:\n",
    "        job = export_to_workspace(cube, collection).create_job(\n",
    "            title=f\"SAR {name} monthly composites (docs)\", job_options={\"stac-version\": \"1.1\"}, log_level=\"debug\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        job.start_and_wait()\n",
    "        cache = {\"id\": job.job_id, \"collection\": collection}\n",
    "\n",
    "    if \"metadata\" not in cache:\n",
    "        capabilities = connection.capabilities()\n",
    "        cache[\"metadata\"] = connection.job(cache[\"id\"]).describe()\n",
    "        cache[\"parameters\"] = {\n",
    "            \"currency\": capabilities.currency(),\n",
    "            \"federation\": capabilities.ext_federation_backend_details(),\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        job_file.write_text(json.dumps(cache, indent=2))\n",
    "    return cache\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def show_job(cache: dict) -> HTML:\n",
    "    return HTML(render_component(\"job\", data=cache[\"metadata\"], parameters=cache[\"parameters\"]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eee7aeed",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Gamma0 (terrain-flattened)\n",
    "\n",
    "We call the function defined above to compute the γ⁰ monthly composite.\n",
    "The openEO job metadata is visualized afterwards, to give you an idea on what you can expect.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "53ad0acf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gamma0 = monthly_composite(\"gamma0-terrain\")"
   ]
  },
  {
